{"id": "clm:0c4130e52069e4c4d4c90b8d89179cb8ec7a683fb49420843c90ebc824887ed2", "type": "statement", "text": "Duplo lists an external waste bin for the DC-746; this is a manufacturer feature claim. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.duplousa.com/product/dc-746-slitter-cutter-creaser/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:694381557d49ce049c0ee022d54bdc990aa852276eef6fbf536456d6c3fad224", "ev:af84b4b59f5bca973e660cc88c799911d9964bb2d38bda3fcafae92fab4dbd2c"]}
{"id": "clm:c077c3eb7ec1f8011b6baef65d526b3531f89035deb5998fc350262552c102f4", "type": "statement", "text": "Lassco states that the CR-50 accepts Standard, Special and Large cutting units and includes one Standard unit. Tool selection is part of configuring the corner-rounding operation. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.lasscowizer.com/cr-50-manual-corner-cutter/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0fac21ed0c7a5b62262f5119f97941be0c7dd925d2a7056ff91d322b79b6486b"]}
{"id": "clm:3916f6105a75e346ed3c3b4793c09eca1df078a19cf16ce029aa2c34b79c1d08", "type": "statement", "text": "The AeroCut X manual warns that overfilled waste can cause errors or breakdown. Waste removal therefore belongs in the cutting workflow. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://mbmcorp.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/AeroCut-X-OPERATION-MANUALinch.pdf", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:476883e6b750212f7e88ff99b1dea73583628bee2d0fd5907f18e37ba3dd5631"]}
{"id": "clm:bf21abf123dc5473cc57c8b219f49840478fe21eb488038d0429fcba25907a17", "type": "statement", "text": "Duplo describes the DC-746 cutting mechanism as rotary slitters plus a guillotine cutter. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.duplousa.com/product/dc-746-slitter-cutter-creaser/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a205de6944e2fa9a877d2d50c7d99abbe4b7cfb0b6b0c25cede098cb7cc1e6e9", "ev:af84b4b59f5bca973e660cc88c799911d9964bb2d38bda3fcafae92fab4dbd2c"]}
{"id": "clm:5027cf4c17d0c2dae7b8b2f0fca792cd17929f8b4c845fbdb5c5a5f7beae43f5", "type": "statement", "text": "MBM’s AeroCut X product page rates speed at 24 sheets/minute for two cuts and one crease on an 8 1/2 × 11 sheet. That rating does not measure completed rounded playing-card decks. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://mbmcorp.com/product/aerocut-x-digital-print-finisher/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "measures", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:aa2afc04cbd8186aa593635d7efa3621a042e32f8196582b513502390d24f804"]}
{"id": "clm:b5a9a4b72d93ce363ee5d05320205b526c66c55d73f7d2a02954f5cc7c33fa63", "type": "statement", "text": "The CR-50 manual rates Standard/Special cutting units for paper stacks up to 1/2 inch and Large cutting units for stacks up to 1/8 inch. The applicable stack limit depends on the installed cutting-unit class. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.lasscowizer.com/cmsb/uploads/cr50-manual-small.pdf", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6bc3ac0d7e47a928d138112b84398a0060ab8a2e415e77b8fbd7edfcf882f748", "ev:e56e83cba2eb3c9108462ef28d833edbc1b30f0b3cf0b8232bdf27eaf2431018"]}
{"id": "clm:b241a046c0107d36ba168f48ac968b5ff4af7d03594bfbe9a201ffcc6578d261", "type": "statement", "text": "Print & Finishing Solutions identifies a nicked blade as a possible cause of ragged slit edges. Treat this as dealer troubleshooting guidance, not a measured failure rate. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.pfsgraphics.com/resources-slitter-cutters-trimmers", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a44799c8adb088660d362f000d48e06b20614feaaa074d4dbb36d1caa3dbc29a"]}
{"id": "clm:aaeef5edd9fd2c82ba4abe4b621af968d63baac5fa3abc2c5516032479098348", "type": "statement", "text": "In an April 2024 PrintPlanet thread, operator COGordon reported Duplo 646 double-feeding on stocks lighter than card stock despite service-company settings. This is an anecdote about that machine, not a failure-rate measurement or evidence against the DC-746. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://printplanet.com/threads/methods-for-reducing-static-on-duplo-646.294079/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.duplousa.com/product/dc-746-slitter-cutter-creaser/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:601411bcff43636314665eb63183e94e7150c8b0c07af71354923b9dd157e9d4", "ev:af84b4b59f5bca973e660cc88c799911d9964bb2d38bda3fcafae92fab4dbd2c"]}
{"id": "clm:3c58b597d924b4614dcd63ecf9c00dbbea4e37513c3e19b26832aa01e7532ead", "type": "statement", "text": "PrintNinja describes a stack smoothing/rounding operation after trimming, while its domestic rotary-die route forms final size and rounded corners together. These are alternative production routes, rather than a requirement that every card use both. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://printninja.com/card-game-production/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:37ef95e27f1611f1aad7189b625cd88238d92d0a87e51270556dc2d34760e6eb"]}
{"id": "clm:06e2c52ff5423a037a66fc11f9d5af993d9f93b43856a6508c62b99082c88dc3", "type": "statement", "text": "The Game Crafter documents die cutting with rounded corners except on its trading-card format, establishing a card-production route that does not require separately rounding rectangular cuts. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://help.thegamecrafter.com/article/85-cards", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:aeb9e12c51cd6f7c5bf4036979e3a4446539baeb08c1dc0c6a12e903aef5de13"]}
{"id": "clm:bc4d1134875f2b7c2bab02194eb8895d6318ebc660213929df0c1a68d4af9d93", "type": "statement", "text": "Duplo lists the DC-746 feeder at 150 mm, stock weight at 110–350 gsm, and maxima of 10 slits and 30 cuts per sheet. These are manufacturer specifications for this model, not measured playing-card production results. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.duplousa.com/product/dc-746-slitter-cutter-creaser/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:af84b4b59f5bca973e660cc88c799911d9964bb2d38bda3fcafae92fab4dbd2c", "ev:ef11b797ecd5128d18ae9f2fcb78e7b3d2b0747b809b2711d1fad422c99c5385"]}
{"id": "clm:e926818a989636daa4729819f8ecdc9fffa6b7f5ad616227a70bc39e8e8e61ac", "type": "statement", "text": "In the AeroCut X manual’s MANUSET layout table, gutter H starts at 0.08 inch depending on paper; entering zero requests single cuts. Layout planning must distinguish a removed gutter from a shared cut. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://mbmcorp.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/AeroCut-X-OPERATION-MANUALinch.pdf", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0fac1c1841027928492ef4834770ba53faa672d54973c9b6e51dec15d65a71ed"]}
{"id": "clm:83269745941cd58001a6ae47763b838ba5434683916002d7c4733e0668ec6270", "type": "statement", "text": "Print & Finishing Solutions warns that heavily static-charged paper can produce misfeeds, double feeds or jams. This dealer’s troubleshooting guidance qualifies expectations of uninterrupted automatic slitting/cutting. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.pfsgraphics.com/resources-slitter-cutters-trimmers", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:9b00e65ac3ffaaf145144ff6dd54ac2f4e4d7d211bd609825811281818bb07b7"]}
{"id": "clm:41f21707b29656a2e7892211b751adb9634d97583f29cc6069b962f6d5292f1b", "type": "statement", "text": "In a December 2021 PrintPlanet discussion about a Duplo 618 cutting crooked, one participant reported similar problems with dirty rollers and said cleaning resolved them. This is an operator anecdote about that model, not a general reliability estimate. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://printplanet.com/threads/duplo-618-slitter-cutter-creaser-problems.291812/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:18696c4606d0c1b3c6fc4eab17fc16657c976d4d17efb8c2fc1514291077702a"]}
{"id": "clm:b837838e839dfe85448d0255e59508530a1254357c2969af3a7c2f473656932d", "type": "statement", "text": "Rollem describes the SlipStream III cutting route as first-direction slitting, with or without bleed, followed by right-angle transfer into the second-direction cutter. This is manufacturer evidence for a two-direction sheet-to-card cutting architecture. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://rollem.com/news/monthly-new-feature-slipstream-cutting-module/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sheet cutting slitting and corner rounding"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:93af020420b77fee09d17029404c3700b3b015fe0c9c0b28cc701eb8123e90f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:9446a8d88e9b9fa53893b5a519cb208702440e9004c27e60dd7ff9cc7667c4ed"]}
